  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "yawn",
      "explanation": "The involuntary opening of the mouth wide with a deep breath, typically when tired or bored."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06484_akubi_ex1",
      "japanese": "{眠|ねむ}くて{欠伸|あくび}が{出|で}る。",
      "english": "I'm sleepy and can't stop yawning.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06484_akubi_ex2",
      "japanese": "{会議中|かいぎちゅう}に{欠伸|あくび}をするのは{失礼|しつれい}だ。",
      "english": "It's rude to yawn during a meeting.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06484_akubi_ex3",
      "japanese": "{大|おお}きな{欠伸|あくび}をしてしまった。",
      "english": "I let out a big yawn.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06484_akubi_ex4",
      "japanese": "{欠伸|あくび}は{伝染|でんせん}すると{言|い}われている。",
      "english": "Yawns are said to be contagious.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06484_akubi_ex5",
      "japanese": "{授業中|じゅぎょうちゅう}に{何度|なんど}も{欠伸|あくび}が{出|で}てしまい、{先生|せんせい}に{注意|ちゅうい}された。",
      "english": "I kept yawning during class and the teacher warned me.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "KANJI: Usually written in hiragana as あくび. The kanji {欠伸|あくび} is rarely used.\n\nVERB USAGE:\n・{欠伸|あくび}をする (to yawn - suru-verb form)\n・{欠伸|あくび}が{出|で}る (to yawn - \"a yawn comes out\")\n・{欠伸|あくび}を{噛|か}み{殺|ころ}す (to stifle a yawn)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n・{大|おお}きな{欠伸|あくび} - a big yawn\n・{生|なま}{欠伸|あくび} - yawning (continuous/repeated)\n・{欠伸|あくび}を{我慢|がまん}する - to hold back a yawn\n\nRELATED INVOLUNTARY BODY ACTIONS:\n・くしゃみ - sneeze\n・しゃっくり - hiccup\n・げっぷ - burp",
